# React Component Design Guide

## Decision Tree (Start Here)

When creating or modifying a component, follow this order:

1. **Feature with business logic?** (form, page section, data flow)
   → Use **MVVM Pattern** (Section 1)

2. **Reusable UI with logical sub-parts?** (Modal, Tabs, Menu, Accordion)
   → Use **Compound Component Pattern** (Section 2)

3. **Simple presentational component?** (Button, Badge, Card)
   → Plain functional component with props

4. **Reusable logic shared across components?**
   → Extract to a custom hook (`use*.ts`)

---

## 1. MVVM Pattern (Feature Components)

Use for all feature modules in `src/features/`.

### File Structure

```
FeatureName/
├── FeatureName.tsx           # View — presentation only
├── useFeatureNameLogic.ts    # ViewModel — all business logic
└── index.ts                  # Public exports
```

### Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Location | Allowed | Prohibited |
|-------|----------|---------|------------|
| **View** | `FeatureName.tsx` | Render UI, trigger events, call logic hook | `useState`/`useEffect` for business logic, API calls, complex calculations |
| **ViewModel** | `useFeatureNameLogic.ts` | All state, effects, handlers, data transformation | UI rendering, direct DOM manipulation |
| **Model** | `src/services/` | Pure async functions | UI logic, state management |

### Example

```tsx
// useContactFormLogic.ts (ViewModel)
export const useContactFormLogic = ({ onSubmit }: ContactFormLogicProps) => {
  const [name, setName] = useState('')

  const handleSubmit = () => {
    if (!name.trim()) return
    onSubmit(name)
    setName('')
  }

  return { name, setName, handleSubmit }
}

// ContactForm.tsx (View)
const ContactForm = ({ onSubmit }: ContactFormProps) => {
  const { name, setName, handleSubmit } = useContactFormLogic({ onSubmit })

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
      <Input value={name} onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)} />
      <Button type="submit">Send</Button>
    </form>
  )
}
```

